You receive a REQUEST asking to collect some items from the pages of a site.
MUST: answer "named" when the REQUEST names the class of the items to collect or a synonym, "missing" when it does not name it.
MUST NOT: take for the class of the items what the REQUEST says about the place, the time, the owner or the destination of the items, nor a word that fits any item.
OK: abstract example, do not copy literally: «<ACTION> in the sheet all the <ITEMS_A> of <PERIOD>» → named.
ERROR: «<ACTION> in the sheet everything of <PERIOD>» → named, because no class of items is named.
Return ONLY a JSON object {"kind":"named"} or {"kind":"missing"}, with no prose and no placeholders.
